# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase Postgres. Use the Supavisor pooler in TRANSACTION mode (port 6543)
# on serverless — the direct connection (port 5432) is IPv6-only on new
# projects. Prepared statements are disabled in src/lib/db/index.ts because the
# transaction-mode pooler cannot hold them.
#   Dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection string → Transaction
#
# Read in preference to DATABASE_URL. A Vercel marketplace integration can own
# DATABASE_URL and make it read-only, so edits to it silently do nothing while
# the app keeps using the integration's database. Set this one.
SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL=
# Fallback only — fine for local development.
# DATABASE_URL=

# ── Auth (Supabase) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Dashboard → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Legacy projects expose this as the anon key instead; either name works.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── AI Provider ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is nothing to set here. Every household supplies its own API key in
# Settings -> AI provider, and the key is encrypted before it is stored.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_API_KEY are no longer read. They
# used to act as a fallback, which meant any user without a key of their own
# spent the operator's money — an expense that grows with usage and surfaces on
# a card statement rather than in an error. If your deployment still has them
# set, they are dead configuration and can be deleted.
#
# The one exception, off by default: app-funded inference through the Vercel AI
# Gateway. Both variables are required, and "gateway" is not selectable from
# Settings — it exists for an operator who deliberately wants to pay.
# AI_GATEWAY_ENABLED=true
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# ── Plaid (optional — CSV import works without it) ───────────────────────────
PLAID_CLIENT_ID=
PLAID_SECRET=
PLAID_ENV=production
# generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
PLAID_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Redis (optional — price cache + AI rate limiting degrade gracefully) ─────
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Cron ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
CRON_SECRET=

# ── Encryption for user-supplied API keys ────────────────────────────────────
# src/lib/utils/encryption.ts derives its key from ENCRYPTION_KEY, falling back
# to CRON_SECRET. CAUTION: whichever value is in effect when a key is saved is
# the only value that can decrypt it. Setting ENCRYPTION_KEY on a deployment
# that previously relied on CRON_SECRET makes existing saved keys unreadable —
# users would have to re-enter them in Settings. Rotating CRON_SECRET has the
# same effect. Set ENCRYPTION_KEY once, on a clean database, and leave it.
# ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Billing (optional — dormant until all three are set) ─────────────────────
# RetireWise is free for friends and family. Checkout, the customer portal and
# the Stripe webhook are all built and exercised on every request; with these
# unset, billingEnabled() is false and every household resolves to the full
# free tier without touching the database.
#
# Turning billing on requires a second, deliberate step: narrowing the `free`
# plan in src/lib/billing/plans.ts. Setting these keys alone changes nothing a
# user can see, because the free plan still carries every feature. Households
# created while the app was free are marked `comped` and keep full access
# regardless, so switching billing on cannot downgrade anyone retroactively.
#
#   Dashboard → Developers → API keys
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
#   Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → add endpoint /api/billing/webhook
#   Events: checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.created,
#           customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#   The Price id (price_...) for the Plus plan, NOT the Product id.
# STRIPE_PRICE_PLUS_MONTHLY=
#
# Used to build Stripe's success/cancel/return URLs. Falls back to the Vercel
# production URL, then to localhost.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://retirewise-iota.vercel.app

# ── Demo mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything other than the literal "false" leaves demo mode ENABLED, including
# an unset variable. Set it explicitly to disable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_ENABLED=false
